{
  "_readme": [
    "ONE table of cases, read by BOTH agent/tests/db-path.test.js and",
    "api/tests/test_db_path.py. It is the only thing keeping",
    "agent/src/utils/db-path.js and api/db_path.py in step.",
    "",
    "They were previously 'kept in step by the tests on each side', which is",
    "how they came to disagree about what a connection string even is: Node",
    "keyed redaction on '://' while Python keyed it on ':/'. Node therefore",
    "printed 'postgresql:/user:PASSWORD@host/db' verbatim -- out of the very",
    "guard whose purpose is to protect it -- while Python mangled the real",
    "Windows path 'C:/Users/x/data.db' into 'C://<redacted>'. Four review",
    "rounds passed over that, because neither suite ever ran the other's",
    "inputs.",
    "",
    "Add a case here, not to one suite. Both sides must agree byte for byte.",
    "",
    "cases[]  input -> expected output of redactCredentials/redact_credentials.",
    "         'connection_string' is also the expected verdict of",
    "         assertFilesystemPath/assert_filesystem_path: true means it must",
    "         throw, false means it must accept. The two share one predicate,",
    "         so one flag pins both.",
    "         'forbidden' lists substrings that must NOT appear in the",
    "         redacted output or in the rejection message.",
    "redos[]  input = unit*count + suffix; must complete within max_ms.",
    "",
    "Non-string inputs (None/null, undefined, 5) are deliberately absent:",
    "str(None) is 'None' but String(null) is 'null', so their coercion is",
    "language-specific and cannot be shared. Each suite covers those locally."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "label": "a plain absolute path",
      "input": "/data/voiceagent.db",
      "expected": "/data/voiceagent.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a path containing '@' — a legal filesystem character",
      "input": "/tmp/a@b/x.db",
      "expected": "/tmp/a@b/x.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a path containing ':' not followed by '/'",
      "input": "/tmp/a:b/x.db",
      "expected": "/tmp/a:b/x.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a dated backup directory, ':' mid-path",
      "input": "/tmp/backup:2026-08-30/x.db",
      "expected": "/tmp/backup:2026-08-30/x.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a relative path",
      "input": "./data/v.db",
      "expected": "./data/v.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a bare filename",
      "input": "voiceagent.db",
      "expected": "voiceagent.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a Windows drive path — one letter, one slash, no '@'",
      "input": "C:/Users/x/data.db",
      "expected": "C:/Users/x/data.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a lower-case Windows drive path",
      "input": "c:/users/x/data.db",
      "expected": "c:/users/x/data.db",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "the empty string",
      "input": "",
      "expected": "",
      "connection_string": false
    },
    {
      "label": "a postgresql URL — the canonical case",
      "input": "postgresql://kinvox:SECRETPW@localhost:5432/kinvox",
      "expected": "postgresql://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRETPW",
        "kinvox:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "the pathlib-collapsed single-slash form — FINDING 1, leaked verbatim on Node",
      "input": "postgresql:/kinvox:SECRETPW@localhost:5432/kinvox",
      "expected": "postgresql://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRETPW",
        "kinvox:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "no scheme at all before ':/' — FINDING 1, leaked verbatim on Node",
      "input": ":/user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "no scheme at all before '://'",
      "input": "://user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a digit-led scheme, single slash",
      "input": "1abc:/user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a digit-led scheme, double slash",
      "input": "1abc://user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a punctuation-led scheme, double slash",
      "input": "$$$://user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a punctuation-led scheme, single slash",
      "input": "$$$:/user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a scheme-shaped run after a real path prefix",
      "input": "/mnt/1x://user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "an embedded scheme after a legitimate-looking directory prefix",
      "input": "/mnt/backups/scp://deploy:SECRET@2024/release.db",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "deploy:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a short postgresql URL",
      "input": "postgresql://u:s@h",
      "expected": "postgresql://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "u:s",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "sqlite:/// — three slashes, no authority, nothing to leak",
      "input": "sqlite:///abs/path.db",
      "expected": "sqlite://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "abs/path.db"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "postgres://",
      "input": "postgres://user:SECRET@host/db",
      "expected": "postgres://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "mysql://",
      "input": "mysql://user:SECRET@host/db",
      "expected": "mysql://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "mongodb://",
      "input": "mongodb://user:SECRET@host/db",
      "expected": "mongodb://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a one-character scheme with an authority — drive-shaped but '//' opens userinfo",
      "input": "a://user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a one-character scheme with a single slash but userinfo — the '@' rule is what catches this",
      "input": "a:/user:SECRET@host",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "user:",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a drive letter followed by '//' is an authority, not a drive",
      "input": "C://Users:SECRET@x",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a real Windows drive prefix in front of a real connection string",
      "input": "C:/Users/x/postgresql://u:SECRET@h",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "SECRET",
        "@"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "a drive-shaped prefix with a SECOND ':/' later is not exempt (fail closed)",
      "input": "C:/a/sub:/b",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": []
    },
    {
      "label": "a lone '://'",
      "input": "://",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": []
    },
    {
      "label": "a lone ':/'",
      "input": ":/",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": []
    },
    {
      "label": "a leading null byte",
      "input": "\u0000abc://x",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": [
        "abc"
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "whitespace padding",
      "input": "   \t ://x   ",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": []
    },
    {
      "label": "a non-ASCII scheme-shaped prefix",
      "input": "ünïcödé://x",
      "expected": "<redacted>://<redacted>",
      "connection_string": true,
      "forbidden": []
    }
  ],
  "redos": [
    {
      "label": "4M scheme characters and no separator at all",
      "unit": "a",
      "count": 4000000,
      "suffix": "",
      "max_ms": 5
    },
    {
      "label": "4M scheme characters followed by a separator",
      "unit": "a",
      "count": 4000000,
      "suffix": "://x",
      "max_ms": 100
    },
    {
      "label": "1M repetitions of 'a://'",
      "unit": "a://",
      "count": 1000000,
      "suffix": "",
      "max_ms": 10
    }
  ]
}
